BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  In the age of the Great Wither, the valley of Aethelgard held only a single bushel of golden g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    rain. Sol, the Keeper of the Seed, stood before the chasm that separated him from the fertil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    e soil of the west. To cast the grain into the void was to risk everything, yet he knew the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    earth would triple any gift entrusted to it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  Luna, the Guardian of the Soil, waited on the far side. She held the power to nurture the harv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    est or bury it in greed. If she kept the bounty for herself, the rains would cease, and the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    valley would crumble into ash. If she returned a portion to Sol, the cycle of life would flo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    urish, and they would both feast in the coming seasons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  Sol cast the seeds. They blossomed into a field of gold, tripled by the grace of the earth. Lu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    na looked upon the abundance. She saw that while she could hold it all, true prosperity was ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    a bridge built on reciprocity. She offered back to Sol a fair share of the harvest. Thus, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    e chasm was bridged, not by stone, but by the quiet understanding that to give is to receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    , and to trust is to survive.) Tj ET
