BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  In the dawn of time, the Great Gardener held five golden seeds, the sum of his labor. Before h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    im flowed the Silver River, an entity of boundless potential. The Gardener knew that to keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (     the seeds was to hoard mere potential, but to cast them into the current was an act of fait) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    h. He knelt and entrusted his seeds to the water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  The River, touched by this offering, surged with ancient magic. For every seed cast into its d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    epths, the current conjured three, swelling the harvest. The River became a vessel of transf) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ormation; it could swallow the wealth, leaving the banks barren, or it could flow back to th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    e Gardener, returning a share of the abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  When the River returned the bounty, the Gardener's fields bloomed with eternal spring, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (     River's path grew wide and deep. But when greed clouded their connection, the growth wither) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ed into silence. Thus, the harmony of the world relies on the rhythm of the gift: to send is) Tj ET
