BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      In the age of the first loom, two weavers, Elara and Kael, sat on opposite banks of a silv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        er river. Elara possessed the raw golden silk, while Kael held the enchanted loom that c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        ould weave threads into destiny. Alone, Elara's silk remained brittle, and Kael's loom s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        tood silent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      The Great Pattern dictated that if Elara cast her silk across the water, the loom would we) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        ave it into robes of light, tripling its value. Yet, trust was a fragile bridge. If Kael) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (         kept the light for himself, the river would drown them both in stagnation. If Elara hel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        d back, the loom would never sing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      One solstice, Elara cast her entire store across the currents. Kael, moved by the faith be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        stowed upon him, returned a share of the radiant cloth that exceeded what the silk alone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         could have produced. Together, they draped the world in shimmering gold. The myth of th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        e weaver's exchange teaches that prosperity is not a vessel to be guarded, but a harvest) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (         to be shared. When one agent risks, and the other honors that risk with fairness, the f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        abric of their world grows stronger, weaving a golden destiny that binds the two in eter) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        nal, prosperous resonance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    reasoning:) Tj ET
