BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      In the age of the Great Wither, the valley of Aethelgard held only a single bushel of gold) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        en grain. Sol, the Keeper of the Seed, stood before the chasm that separated him from th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        e fertile soil of the west. To cast the grain into the void was to risk everything, yet ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        he knew the earth would triple any gift entrusted to it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      Luna, the Guardian of the Soil, waited on the far side. She held the power to nurture the ) Tj ET
