BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      In the dawn of time, the Great Gardener held five golden seeds, the sum of his labor. Befo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        re him flowed the Silver River, an entity of boundless potential. The Gardener knew that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         to keep the seeds was to hoard mere potential, but to cast them into the current was an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         act of faith. He knelt and entrusted his seeds to the water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The River, touched by this offering, surged with ancient magic. For every seed cast into i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ts depths, the current conjured three, swelling the harvest. The River became a vessel o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        f transformation; it could swallow the wealth, leaving the banks barren, or it could flo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        w back to the Gardener, returning a share of the abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      When the River returned the bounty, the Gardener's fields bloomed with eternal spring, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         the River's path grew wide and deep. But when greed clouded their connection, the growt) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        h withered into silence. Thus, the harmony of the world relies on the rhythm of the gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        : to send is to invite prosperity, and to return is to honor the bond. They learned that) Tj ET
