BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      In the dawn of time, Aeter and Mura stood at the edge of the Infinite Furrow. Aeter held f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        ive golden seeds, the currency of existence. To plant them alone would yield nothing; th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        e soil required the touch of Mura's hands. Aeter entrusted all five seeds to Mura, watch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        ing as the magic of the earth tripled their number, turning them into fifteen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
