BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      The Stream, ever-moving, knew that if it kept the woven gold for its own depths, the valle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (        y would dry and the Weaver would cease to cast. But if the Stream returned the tapestry,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (         the Weaver would weave again, and the valley would overflow with life. It was a delicat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        e dance; the Weaver provided the spark, and the Stream provided the vessel for growth. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        hey understood that the true secret of the valley was not the accumulation of fibers, bu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        t the grace of the cycle itself. If the Weaver held back, the waters grew still. If the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        Stream hoarded, the threads vanished. But when both acted with open hands, the valley bl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        ossomed into a paradise where the threads never ran thin and the waters never stopped fl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        owing. They were partners in a rhythmic expansion, proving that life grows only when we ) Tj ET
